WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.571
<v Jordan Ruiz>Hi Beth, this is Jordan from Cascadence — we help companies automate data pipelines between systems like your POS and warehouse. Do you have a couple minutes?</v>

00:00:12.271 --> 00:00:24.271
<v Beth Ramirez>I can give you a minute, but I'll save you the pitch — we actually just signed a two-year contract with another vendor last month for exactly that.</v>

00:00:24.971 --> 00:00:35.257
<v Jordan Ruiz>Ah, good to know, and congrats on getting that sorted. Mind if I ask who you went with, just so I understand the landscape?</v>

00:00:35.957 --> 00:00:44.529
<v Beth Ramirez>I'd rather not say, but it's a reasonably well-known platform. Nothing against you specifically, the timing just didn't line up.</v>

00:00:45.229 --> 00:00:56.371
<v Jordan Ruiz>Totally understand, that happens. Would it be alright if I check back in down the line, closer to when that contract would be up for renewal?</v>

00:00:57.071 --> 00:01:03.500
<v Beth Ramirez>Sure, that's fine. Circle back in a couple years and we'll see where things stand.</v>

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.914
<v Jordan Ruiz>Will do, appreciate you taking the call. Have a good one.</v>

00:01:09.614 --> 00:01:10.471
<v Beth Ramirez>You too.</v>
